      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-esc">Escalation path (26%):</strong> IRGC enforcement of the July 2 route warning (F12 YES) combined with the IAEA access stalemate causing breakdown of the MOU framework before August 17 is the primary escalation pathway.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path (55%):</strong> Khamenei funeral delay, IAEA stalemate, and the absence of a confirmed HLC date collectively drive the most probable outcome: neither breakthrough nor breakdown through August 31, with Hormuz transits rising below the 30/day threshold.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path (19%):</strong> A face-saving IAEA access formula agreed post-July 9 enabling an HLC meeting before July 23 (F13) and a final deal before August 17 (F10) is possible but requires all three current obstacles to clear in sequence.</p>
